hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18932","Waki narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from his brother, from Abu Kahil, Ismail said: I saw Abu Kahil, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressing the people on the day of Eid on a slit-nostriled she-camel, while an Abyssinian was holding its bridle."
